unitotem-manager (3.0.0~dev10) stable; urgency=medium

  * Window layout: a window has a content area (blank margins, in percent of the
    window, replaces the old xinit window geometry) and can be split into panes like
    Konsole's split view, each pane with its own playlist; editor on the Viewers page
    (admin), orientation and flip of each window are reported and kept across restarts
  * RSS ticker: several sources with their own interval merged in one list, a bar per
    window (Rich markup with f-string style fields, count/today/range selection, one or
    two lanes, clock at the start or end, overlay or reserved space) scrolled by the
    compositor (no jumps); new dependency python3-feedparser
  * Screens: DPMS is the first choice to switch a screen on or off; a screen switched
    off over DDC/CEC/serial is remembered and woken with the right sequence (DDC: 05
    then 01); the UI shows "off (DDC)"

 -- Alessandro Campolo <campolo.alex@gmail.com>  Sun, 25 Oct 2026 22:40:00 +0100

unitotem-manager (3.0.0~dev9) stable; urgency=medium

  * unitotem-viewer: the base labwc configuration moves from /etc/unitotem/xdg to
    /usr/share/unitotem/xdg: an A/B update imports all of /etc/unitotem from the
    previous slot, which froze an image-owned file at its first-install version
    (the dev8 fix of the empty <name> never reached an updated board).
    /etc/unitotem holds user and device state only
  * Viewer: editing the volume or mute of the asset on screen applies at once
    (SetAssetAudio), no new showing needed
  * Viewer: commands sent to a window before its page is loaded (a window restored
    to its playlist at start) wait for the load instead of being lost

