unitotem-manager (3.0.0~dev6) stable; urgency=medium

  * The kiosk runs on Wayland (labwc) and nothing else: no X server, no
    python3-xlib, no xrandr/xset. unitotem-viewer ships the compositor service
    (unitotem-compositor.service, enabled by the image) and the base
    configuration of labwc; unitotem-node drops 10-x11.conf for 10-wayland.conf
  * Screens, screen power, touch mapping and the screen-in-the-browser use the
    compositor (wlr-randr, wlopm, labwc configuration fragments, wayvnc)
  * Output names are the compositor's (HDMI-A-1): saved assignments and
    settings follow by themselves; the screen mechanism "x" is now "output"
  * The Display page no longer moves a window onto a clicked monitor

 -- Alessandro Campolo <campolo.alex@gmail.com>  Tue, 20 Oct 2026 22:40:00 +0200

unitotem-manager (3.0.0~dev5) stable; urgency=medium

  * Split by role: unitotem-manager is a complete orchestrator on its own;
    the machine integration (network, audio, displays, power, timers,
    updates, terminal, hotspot) is unitotem-node and the local windows are
    unitotem-viewer, both plugins of the core; "unitotem" installs all three
  * No bundled virtualenv: runs on the system Python with Debian packages
  * Timers run inside UniTotem (croniter), not in the system crontab
  * Backup, restore and reset by selectable parts, including the pairing
    keys and certificates; GET /backup was answering the web page
  * The service is Type=notify: an early Qt splash is on screen before CEF
    starts and READY=1 is sent at that point (or when the web server
    answers, without local windows)
  * The service now fails, and is restarted, when the X server goes away
  * DPMS is set by the viewer itself through python-xlib

 -- Alessandro Campolo <campolo.alex@gmail.com>  Tue, 13 Oct 2026 10:00:00 +0200

